# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plugging into ffsim’s simulation interface {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"
msgstr "Menyambung ke antara muka simulasi ffsim {#plugging-into-ffsims-simulation-interface}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) is a high-performance simulator for fermionic quantum circuits that exploits particle number and spin-Z conservation to represent state vectors more compactly than a generic $2^n$-dimensional qubit statevector. It defines protocols that any object can implement to participate in its simulation machinery (see [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") for this package’s own protocols, which follow the same design):\n"
msgstr "[ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/) ialah simulator berprestasi tinggi untuk litar kuantum fermionik yang mengeksploitasi pemuliharaan bilangan zarah dan spin-Z untuk mewakili vektor keadaan dengan lebih padat daripada vektor keadaan qubit generik berdimensi $2^n$. Ia mentakrifkan protokol yang boleh dilaksanakan oleh mana-mana objek untuk mengambil bahagian dalam jentera simulasinya (lihat [`qiskit_fermions.protocols`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/protocols#module-qiskit_fermions.protocols \"qiskit_fermions.protocols\") untuk protokol pakej ini sendiri, yang mengikut reka bentuk yang sama):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, applying the object as a unitary to a fixed-particle-number state vector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary.html#ffsim.SupportsApplyUnitary \"(in ffsim)\"), melalui kaedah `_apply_unitary_(vec, norb, nelec, copy)`, yang mengenakan objek sebagai unitari pada vektor keadaan bilangan zarah tetap\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, returning a [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") view of the object on that same sector\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), melalui kaedah `_linear_operator_(norb, nelec)`, yang mengembalikan pandangan [`scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") bagi objek pada sektor yang sama\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), by the method `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, returning the object’s trace on that sector.\n"
msgstr "[`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\"), melalui kaedah `_trace_(norb, nelec)`, yang mengembalikan surih objek pada sektor tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This package implements that interface: every fermionic gate in [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") provides `_apply_unitary_`, and [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") provides `_linear_operator_` and `_trace_`. That is what makes this package’s operators and circuits *compatible* with ffsim, so its tools work on them natively, with no conversion step. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") can simulate a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") end to end, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") can diagonalize a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), and sampling utilities like [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (used in the [SKQD guide](skqd#skqd-getting-started) to turn a simulated statevector into measurement counts) work without modification.\n"
msgstr "Pakej ini melaksanakan antara muka itu: setiap Gate fermionik dalam [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") menyediakan `_apply_unitary_`, dan [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") menyediakan `_linear_operator_` dan `_trace_`. Itulah yang menjadikan operator dan litar pakej ini *serasi* dengan ffsim, jadi alatnya berfungsi pada mereka secara asli, tanpa langkah penukaran. [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") boleh mensimulasikan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") dari hujung ke hujung, [`ffsim.linear_operator()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.linear_operator.html#ffsim.linear_operator \"(in ffsim)\") boleh mempepenjurukan [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\"), dan utiliti pensampelan seperti [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\") (digunakan dalam [panduan SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) untuk menukarkan vektor keadaan tersimulasi kepada kiraan pengukuran) berfungsi tanpa pengubahsuaian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What `_linear_operator_` returns is an ordinary SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), so [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") and friends work on it too.\n"
msgstr "Apa yang dikembalikan oleh `_linear_operator_` ialah [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") SciPy biasa, jadi [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") dan fungsi sepertinya juga berfungsi padanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coupling through ffsim’s protocols is what buys this: its actively developed ecosystem of simulation and sampling utilities applies to this package’s circuits and operators unchanged, and users already working with ffsim can mix in this package’s gates and operators without learning another simulation API.\n"
msgstr "Gandingan melalui protokol ffsim inilah yang memberikan manfaat ini: ekosistem utiliti simulasi dan pensampelannya yang dibangunkan secara aktif terpakai pada litar dan operator pakej ini tanpa perubahan, dan pengguna yang sudah bekerja dengan ffsim boleh mencampurkan Gate dan operator pakej ini tanpa mempelajari API simulasi lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is an optional dependency {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"
msgstr "ffsim ialah kebergantungan pilihan {#ffsim-is-an-optional-dependency}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim is declared as an optional extra (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, or transitively by `[all]`), guarded at runtime by [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (as was shown above). Installing it unlocks simulation: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") and [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") are implemented by converting this package’s [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") into an [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), so without ffsim they raise [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Everything that does not simulate (building operators, mapping them, and transpiling the resulting circuits) needs none of it.\n"
msgstr "ffsim diisytiharkan sebagai tambahan pilihan (`pip install \"qiskit-fermions[ffsim]\"`, atau secara transitif oleh `[all]`), dikawal pada masa larian oleh [`HAS_FFSIM`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/utils-optionals#qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM \"qiskit_fermions.utils.optionals.HAS_FFSIM\") (seperti yang ditunjukkan di atas). Memasangnya membuka simulasi: [`ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator.html#ffsim.SupportsLinearOperator \"(in ffsim)\") dan [`ffsim.SupportsTrace`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.SupportsTrace.html#ffsim.SupportsTrace \"(in ffsim)\") dilaksanakan dengan menukarkan [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") pakej ini kepada [`ffsim.FermionOperator`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.FermionOperator.html#ffsim.FermionOperator \"(in ffsim)\"), jadi tanpa ffsim ia menimbulkan [`MissingOptionalLibraryError`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/exceptions#qiskit.exceptions.MissingOptionalLibraryError). Segala yang tidak mensimulasikan (membina operator, memetakannya, dan mentranspil litar yang terhasil) tidak memerlukannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fermionic simulation lives in a fixed particle-number sector {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"
msgstr "Simulasi fermionik berlaku dalam sektor bilangan zarah tetap {#fermionic-simulation-lives-in-a-fixed-particle-number-sector}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both `_apply_unitary_` and `_linear_operator_` take an `nelec` argument and represent the state vector over the *fixed-particle-number determinant basis* for that `(norb, nelec)` sector, mirroring ffsim’s (and, transitively, PySCF’s) FCI space setup, rather than the full $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$-dimensional space a general qubit simulator would use. This is a much smaller space (its size is a product of binomial coefficients rather than a power of two), but it comes with a hard restriction. Only operators and gates that preserve particle number (and, in the spinful case, each spin species’ particle number individually) can be represented in it. An operator whose action would move amplitude to a different particle number has nowhere to put it.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua `_apply_unitary_` dan `_linear_operator_` menerima argumen `nelec` dan mewakili vektor keadaan pada *asas penentu bilangan zarah tetap* bagi sektor `(norb, nelec)` itu, mencerminkan penyediaan ruang FCI ffsim (dan, secara transitif, PySCF), dan bukannya ruang berdimensi $2^{\\text{num\\_modes}}$ penuh yang akan digunakan oleh simulator qubit am. Ini ruang yang jauh lebih kecil (saiznya ialah hasil darab pekali binomial dan bukan kuasa dua), tetapi ia disertai sekatan keras. Hanya operator dan Gate yang mengekalkan bilangan zarah (dan, dalam kes berspin, bilangan zarah setiap spesies spin secara individu) boleh diwakili di dalamnya. Operator yang tindakannya akan memindahkan amplitud ke bilangan zarah yang berbeza tidak mempunyai tempat untuk meletakkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ffsim resolves this by rejecting such an operator outright: converting one to a linear operator raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) naming which conservation law fails. That is the right default, because applying $\\exp(-i t H)$ for a Hamiltonian $H$ with a non-particle-conserving term would otherwise turn a would-be unitary into a non-unitary, physically-meaningless map.\n"
msgstr "ffsim menyelesaikan ini dengan menolak operator sedemikian secara terus: menukarkannya kepada operator linear menimbulkan [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) yang menamakan hukum pemuliharaan mana yang gagal. Itu lalai yang betul, kerana mengenakan $\\exp(-i t H)$ bagi Hamiltonian $H$ dengan sebutan yang tidak memelihara zarah sebaliknya akan menukarkan pemetaan yang sepatutnya unitari menjadi pemetaan tidak unitari yang tidak bermakna dari segi fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") surfaces that rejection from the operator it evolves.\n"
msgstr "[`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") memunculkan penolakan itu daripada operator yang dievolusikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") checks that its (embedded) rotation matrix is block-diagonal across the alpha/beta split in the spinful case, and raises a [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) if it mixes spin sectors.\n"
msgstr "[`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") memeriksa bahawa matriks putaran (terbenam) bersifat pepenjuru blok merentasi pembahagian alfa/beta dalam kes berspin, dan menimbulkan [`ValueError`](https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError) jika ia mencampurkan sektor spin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-particle-preserving simulation is therefore out of reach in fermionic space, by construction of the fixed-sector representation, and that is the price of the compact FCI space which makes fermionic simulation tractable in the first place. If your algorithm needs particle-number-violating operators (for example, a qubit-native error channel, or an operator built for a mapped Hamiltonian that does not conserve particle numbers term by term), transpile to qubits first and simulate the resulting [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) with a qubit-level simulator instead. Any transpilation route works for this; the [fermionic circuit](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) and [transpilation](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guides go into more detail, but [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") is a reasonable default choice.\n"
msgstr "Oleh itu, simulasi yang tidak mengekalkan zarah berada di luar jangkauan dalam ruang fermionik, mengikut reka bentuk perwakilan sektor tetap, dan itulah harga bagi ruang FCI padat yang menjadikan simulasi fermionik boleh dilaksanakan pada asalnya. Jika algoritma anda memerlukan operator yang melanggar bilangan zarah (contohnya, saluran ralat asli-qubit, atau operator yang dibina untuk Hamiltonian terpeta yang tidak mengekalkan bilangan zarah bagi setiap sebutan), transpilasikan ke qubit terlebih dahulu dan simulasikan [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) yang terhasil dengan simulator peringkat qubit. Mana-mana laluan transpilasi berfungsi untuk ini; panduan [litar fermionik](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation) dan [transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) menerangkan dengan lebih terperinci, tetapi [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") ialah pilihan lalai yang munasabah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The block-spin convention for spinful systems {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"
msgstr "Konvensyen spin blok untuk sistem berspin {#the-block-spin-convention-for-spinful-systems}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`nelec` is typed `int | tuple[int, int]`, and its type, not a separate flag, is what selects one of the supported mode layouts:\n"
msgstr "`nelec` ditaip sebagai `int | tuple[int, int]`, dan jenisnya, bukan bendera berasingan, yang memilih salah satu reka letak mod yang disokong:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An **int** selects the **spinless** interpretation. The `norb` modes are treated directly as spinless orbitals, and `nelec` is the total particle count.\n"
msgstr "**int** memilih tafsiran **tanpa spin**. `norb` mod dilayan secara langsung sebagai orbital tanpa spin, dan `nelec` ialah jumlah bilangan zarah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **pair** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` selects the **spinful** interpretation of `2 * norb` modes under a fixed **block-spin convention**. Modes `0 .. norb` are the alpha (spin-up) orbitals and modes `norb .. 2 * norb` are the beta (spin-down) orbitals. Each spin species is conserved *independently*; an alpha-only term can move an electron between alpha modes but never into a beta mode, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr "**Pasangan** `(n_alpha, n_beta)` memilih tafsiran **berspin** bagi `2 * norb` mod di bawah **konvensyen spin blok** yang tetap. Mod `0 .. norb` ialah orbital alfa (spin-atas) dan mod `norb .. 2 * norb` ialah orbital beta (spin-bawah). Setiap spesies spin dikekalkan *secara bebas*; sebutan alfa sahaja boleh memindahkan elektron antara mod alfa tetapi tidak sekali-kali ke dalam mod beta, dan sebaliknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This dispatch happens at every ffsim-protocol entry point in this package (gate constructors, `_apply_unitary_placed_` implementations, and the native Rust kernel’s sector compilation), and it is the convention used throughout the [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) and [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) guides (for example, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") fills alpha occupations into modes `0 .. n_alpha` and beta occupations into modes `norb .. norb + n_beta`). It is worth contrasting this with the [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") in general, which use *generic* mode indices with no inherent spin semantics (see the [fermionic circuit guide](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). The block-spin meaning is imposed only when a spinful `nelec` is supplied to a simulation call, not baked into the operator or circuit representation itself.\n"
msgstr "Pengagihan ini berlaku pada setiap titik masuk protokol ffsim dalam pakej ini (pembina gate, pelaksanaan `_apply_unitary_placed_`, dan kompilasi sektor kernel Rust asli), dan ia ialah konvensyen yang digunakan dalam panduan [LUCJ](lucj#lucj-transpilation) dan [SKQD](skqd#skqd-getting-started) (contohnya, [`InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes.from_hartree_fock\") mengisi penghunian alfa ke dalam mod `0 .. n_alpha` dan penghunian beta ke dalam mod `norb .. norb + n_beta`). Ia wajar dibezakan dengan modul [`qiskit_fermions.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") dan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") secara amnya, yang menggunakan indeks mod *generik* tanpa semantik spin yang wujud (lihat [panduan litar fermionik](circuit#fermionic-circuit-explanation)). Maksud spin blok hanya dikenakan apabila `nelec` berspin dibekalkan kepada panggilan simulasi, bukan terterap dalam perwakilan operator atau litar itu sendiri.\n"

